WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.449
Hydrogen could power Nordic buses, trucks, ships and industry.

2
00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:08.331
Yet one question keeps coming back: where do we store it?

3
00:00:08.731 --> 00:00:11.456
Hydrogen is the lightest gas there is.

4
00:00:11.466 --> 00:00:17.136
Even at five hundred bar, one kilogram needs about thirty litres of costly tank.

5
00:00:17.146 --> 00:00:22.956
So local systems add storage at every site, and pay for hydrogen that sits idle.

6
00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.090
But storage is a symptom, not the cause.

7
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.030
Production follows the wind.

8
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:30.707
Demand follows buses, trucks and ships.

9
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:33.058
Tanks fill the gap between them.

10
00:00:33.458 --> 00:00:44.558
The real question is: how can digital twins help local hydrogen systems produce, move and use hydrogen with minimum storage and maximum business value?

11
00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:48.120
Picture a coastal region in northern Finland.

12
00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:55.983
Two electrolysers, a bus depot, a truck station, an industrial plant and a port, linked by seven tube trailers.

13
00:00:56.383 --> 00:01:02.168
The digital twin mirrors all of it: weather, prices, demand, every trailer and every tank.

14
00:01:02.178 --> 00:01:09.383
Each hour it plans two days ahead: when to produce, what to move, and where to keep a small reserve on wheels.

15
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:18.671
Now we stress one winter month: a cold snap at minus twenty-eight, three calm, expensive days, a snowstorm, and an electrolyser trip.

16
00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:24.780
With the same small tanks, a fixed timetable leaves users without fuel for sixty-two hours.

17
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.783
The twin supplies them all.

18
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:39.295
Compared with a storage-first design, it needs ninety-two per cent less stationary storage, holds two thirds less hydrogen, and earns about seventy thousand euros more each month.

19
00:01:39.695 --> 00:01:42.808
Hydrogen storage is not only a tank problem.

20
00:01:42.818 --> 00:01:45.585
It is a logistics intelligence problem.

21
00:01:45.595 --> 00:01:48.024
Explore the live twin for yourself.
